+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` with Node.js 20 or newer to serve the homepage and newsletter endpoint. `PORT` defaults to `11222`; `HOST` defaults to `0.0.0.0`.
+
+Newsletter signups are validated and saved as JSON lines in `data/newsletter.jsonl`. Set `DATA_DIR` to a private persistent directory in production and protect/back up that directory. The server only serves the homepage and two explicitly allowed assets, so signup data is never exposed as a static file. This endpoint stores signups; it does not send newsletter campaigns.
+
+Every response includes a Content Security Policy. Scripts require a fresh per-response nonce, styles load from this server, photos load from this server or `https://images.unsplash.com`, and connections and form submissions target this server. Other resource types, framing, and base URL overrides are blocked. Keep these headers when deploying behind a proxy. CSP restricts resource requests; it does not guarantee protection from every possible data leak (for example, top-level navigation).
+
+The form shows a message on network errors, blocked connections, server errors, and requests that exceed ten seconds. Without JavaScript, the form submits directly and the server returns a plain-text confirmation or error.
